        "url": "https://read.qxmd.com/read/21225489/a-comparison-of-muscle-activity-and-1-rm-strength-of-three-chest-press-exercises-with-different-stability-requirements"
      }
    ],
    "safety": {
      "cautions": [
        "Get into position safely: sit on the end of the bench with the dumbbells on the thighs, then lie back and kick them up one knee at a time; at the end of the set bring them back to the thighs or lower them to the floor beside the bench rather than dropping them (clinical opinion).",
        "Hold the dumbbells firmly together over the chest; use fixed-plate dumbbells.",
        "Keep the wrists straight over the forearms; bent-back wrists under a heavy dumbbell strain the wrist.",
        "Stop if sharp pain, numbness or tingling occurs.",
        "Muscle glow colours and activation curves are illustrative, not measured EMG."
      ],
      "modify": [
        "Wrist discomfort: let the dumbbells separate a few centimetres.",
        "Shoulder discomfort: shorten the range so the dumbbells stop just above the chest."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "Close-grip push-up on a bench (incline).",
        "Dumbbell floor press, close grip."
      ],
      "progressions": [
        "Heavier dumbbells.",
        "Pause 1-2 s on the chest.",
        "Incline close-grip press."
      ]
    },
    "muscleNotes": {
      "pec_r": "Presses the arms up and squeezes them together. Grip width did not change overall pectoralis activity in the barbell bench press (Saeterbakken 2021), although the sternal (middle) fibres were less active with a narrow (50% of shoulder width) barbell grip in Muyor 2023.",
      "pec_l": "Presses the arms up and squeezes them together. Grip width did not change overall pectoralis activity in the barbell bench press (Saeterbakken 2021), although the sternal (middle) fibres were less active with a narrow (50% of shoulder width) barbell grip in Muyor 2023.",
      "ant_deltoid_r": "Flexes the shoulder; its activity did not differ between narrow and wide grips (Saeterbakken 2021).",
      "ant_deltoid_l": "Flexes the shoulder; its activity did not differ between narrow and wide grips (Saeterbakken 2021).",
      "triceps_r": "Main elbow extensor: triceps activity was higher with a narrow barbell grip than a wide one (Saeterbakken 2021; Muyor 2023: about 16% vs 12% of MVIC at 50% vs 150% of shoulder width).",
      "triceps_l": "Main elbow extensor: triceps activity was higher with a narrow barbell grip than a wide one (Saeterbakken 2021; Muyor 2023: about 16% vs 12% of MVIC at 50% vs 150% of shoulder width).",
      "serratus_r": "Holds the shoulder blades against the rib cage while each arm moves on its own.",
      "serratus_l": "Holds the shoulder blades against the rib cage while each arm moves on its own.",
      "biceps_r": "Less active with a narrow grip than a wide one (Saeterbakken 2021); still steadies the elbow under the free weights.",
      "biceps_l": "Less active with a narrow grip than a wide one (Saeterbakken 2021); still steadies the elbow under the free weights.",
      "forearm_flexors_r": "Grip the dumbbell handles.",
      "forearm_flexors_l": "Grip the dumbbell handles.",
      "infraspinatus_r": "Rotator cuff: centres the head of the upper arm while the dumbbells balance freely (clinical opinion).",
      "infraspinatus_l": "Rotator cuff: centres the head of the upper arm while the dumbbells balance freely (clinical opinion).",
      "rhomboids_midtrap_r": "Keep the shoulder blades drawn back and down on the bench.",
      "rhomboids_midtrap_l": "Keep the shoulder blades drawn back and down on the bench.",
      "core": "Bracing keeps the ribs down and the pelvis on the seat."
    }
  },
